const faqEn=[
 ['What is an HS Code, and why does it matter?','An HS Code is the international customs classification for a product. It affects duties, permits, restrictions and the information used in declarations.'],
 ['What is a Bill of Lading (B/L)?','A Bill of Lading acknowledges receipt of sea cargo and records the shipper, consignee, goods and carriage terms.'],
 ['How is chargeable weight calculated?','Air freight normally uses the higher of actual weight and volumetric weight. The carrier’s applicable conversion factor must be confirmed.'],
 ['How long will my shipment take?','Transit depends on origin, destination, mode, carrier schedule, customs and cargo acceptance. Our team confirms an estimate with the quote.'],
 ['Can I track my shipment?','Yes. Tracking availability depends on the carrier and service. Our team provides milestone updates and relevant tracking references.'],
 ['What should I prepare to import goods into Dubai?','Usually a commercial invoice, packing list, transport document, importer details, HS Codes and any commodity-specific permits.'],
 ['What documents are required for a personal export from the UAE?','Requirements vary, but commonly include identity documents, a detailed packing list, shipment instructions and destination documents.'],
 ['What documents are required for a commercial export?','Commercial invoice, packing list, export declaration, transport document and any certificates or permits applicable to the goods.'],
 ['Who handles customs clearance and duties?','We coordinate clearance with approved brokers. Duties, taxes and official charges are payable as stated in the quotation and customs assessment.'],
 ['What documents are needed to ship a vehicle?','Vehicle registration, ownership or export certificate, identity documents and destination-specific import approvals may be required.'],
 ['Can personal belongings remain inside the vehicle?','Carrier and destination rules vary. Personal effects are often restricted in vehicles and must never be loaded without written approval.'],
 ['Can you ship dangerous goods?','Yes, subject to SDS review, correct classification, approved packaging, documentation, route and carrier acceptance.'],
 ['How should high-value cargo such as gold be arranged?','High-value cargo requires advance declaration, specialist security, carrier acceptance and suitable insurance arrangements.'],
 ['What items are prohibited or restricted?','Rules vary by country and carrier. Never ship undeclared weapons, illegal goods, dangerous substances or restricted products.'],
 ['Do you offer door-to-door shipping?','Yes. Door-to-door solutions can include collection, freight, clearance coordination and final delivery.'],
 ['Is cargo insurance included?','Not automatically. Cargo insurance can be arranged subject to declared value, cargo, route and policy terms.'],
 ['What should I do if cargo is damaged or missing?','Notify us immediately, keep packaging, take photographs and provide the transport and value documents required for review.'],
 ['Why can a shipment be delayed?','Weather, carrier changes, port congestion, customs inspections, document issues and destination events can affect schedules.']
];
